WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.185
A game ends. The learning should not.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.364
Meet Gambit: a chess opponent and coach, inside Hermes.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.637
You move. One reply. Choose Normal for a quiet game, or Coach for

00:00:18.637 --> 00:00:21.846
explanations. Ask for a hint when you need one.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.319
Bring your own history. Search Chess dot com or Lichess, then choose

00:00:30.319 --> 00:00:31.398
the exact match.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.792
Replay each decision with coaching in chat. Here, Hermes explains a

00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:44.966
recorded move using Stockfish analysis. The board and the conversation

00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:45.801
stay connected.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.402
Now try another idea. Follow the original for its recorded reply.

00:00:54.402 --> 00:00:58.805
Change your move for a calculated response. Your original game stays

00:00:58.805 --> 00:00:59.205
saved.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.512
Resign. GG. Fireworks. And you are ready for the next game.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.871
Eighty two tests. Sixteen Hermes checks. Built to keep playing.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.261
Next: recurring mistakes and targeted practice. Future ideas, built

00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:24.937
around your own games. Today: play, replay, understand.
